1
00:03:41,052 --> 00:03:47,052
You'll Shake!--Quake! Laff, and Laff Some More

2
00:07:22,105 --> 00:07:28,105
Heart to Heart is a comedy film directed by William Beaudine.

3
00:11:03,157 --> 00:11:09,157
Princess Delatorre, young and beautiful widow of an Italian scion of royalty, returns with
her fortune to the small American town where she grew up as Ellen Gutherie.

4
00:14:44,210 --> 00:14:50,210
Arriving by train a few days earlier than she
planned, Ellen is mistaken for Mrs.

5
00:18:25,263 --> 00:18:31,263
Arden, a seamstress of doubtful repute from a neighboring town.

6
00:22:06,315 --> 00:22:12,315
She carries on the deception for fun when her nearsighted
Aunt Katie and others believe she is Mrs.

7
00:25:47,368 --> 00:25:53,368
Phil, her old sweetheart, recognizes her, however, and shows her his new invention,
a corkscrew that turns itself--a failure because of prohibition.

8
00:29:28,421 --> 00:29:34,421
Ellen leaves, having heard how much store is set on her coming; she returns on the proper train,
elaborately made up as Princess Delatorre, and the big reception takes place as planned.

9
00:33:09,473 --> 00:33:15,473
Then she and Phil return to Italy, where they
expect the corkscrew to be a success.

10
00:36:50,526 --> 00:36:56,526
Princess Delatorre / Ellen Guthrie, played by Mary Astor.

11
00:40:31,578 --> 00:40:37,578
Philip Lennox, played by Lloyd Hughes.

12
00:44:12,631 --> 00:44:18,631
Aunt Katie Boyd, played by Louise Fazenda.

13
00:47:53,684 --> 00:47:59,684
Uncle Joe Boyd, played by Lucien Littlefield.

14
00:51:34,736 --> 00:51:40,736
Ruby Boyd, played by Thelma Todd.

15
00:55:15,789 --> 00:55:21,789
Milt D'Arcy, played by Raymond McKee.

16
00:58:56,842 --> 00:59:02,842
Heart to Heart is a 1928 American silent comedy film directed by William
Beaudine and produced and distributed by the First National company.

17
01:02:37,894 --> 01:02:43,894
The film is preserved in the Library of Congress  collection, Packard Campus.

18
01:06:18,947 --> 01:06:24,947
The tone is lighthearted.
